{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Solids, liquids and gases","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Solid"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A solid keeps its own shape and does not flow. A wooden block is a solid."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Liquid"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A liquid flows and takes the shape of its container, but its volume stays the same. Water is a liquid."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a solid?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A rock","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Milk","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Steam","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"cloud"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which of these is a gas?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Air","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Honey","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which group contains only liquids?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Water, oil, juice","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Wood, glass, iron","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Air, steam, oxygen","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You are packing a school trip bag. You can take a bottle of water or a bag of sand. Which do you choose?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"The bottle of water","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"The bag of sand","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Water is a liquid. It flows into your bottle and keeps its volume. Good choice for a long walk!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Sand is a solid made of tiny grains. It is heavy and stays in its shape in the bag. It is not a drink!"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What happens to a liquid in a tall, thin glass if you pour it into a wide dish?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"It spreads out to take the dish's shape","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"It keeps the shape of the glass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"It turns into a solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which material can you put in a balloon and squash into a smaller space?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Air","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Stone","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the solids, liquids and gases lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You can now compare and group materials by their state."}],"actions":[]}}
